# Builds indilib/pyindi-client's 2.2.0 PyPI release, linked against
# indi-stable-core rather than any system libindi -- DESIGN.md's "SWIG
# bindings will not compile against mismatched headers" is why this
# component is in scope at all. See DESIGN.md, "pyindi-client -- packaging
# decisions", 2026-08-26, for why 2.2.0 (an untagged commit on upstream's
# master) is built instead of the last real git tag, v2.1.2 -- that tag
# needs a static libindiclient.a this project's core/ does not build.
#
# The private RPATH baked into the compiled extension at link time
# (pyindi-client/deb/rules) is what keeps this coexisting the same way
# every other component does. The built module itself installs to the
# ordinary system Python location, not /opt/indi-stable -- deliberately, not
# an oversight; see DESIGN.md's same section for why that is not an
# exception to the coexistence rule.

Package: indi-stable-pyindi-client
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: Python bindings for the INDI client library (indi-stable build)
 SWIG-generated Python bindings for INDI's C++ client API
 (INDI::BaseClient et al.), built and version-matched against this
 project's own indi-stable-core rather than any system libindi.
 .
 This is indilib/pyindi-client's own upstream binding, rebuilt against
 this project's private INDI prefix; it is not a fork.
 .
 Unofficial third-party build; not affiliated with or endorsed by the
 INDI project.
